Initial Breakdown
This audit evaluates the electrochemical facsimile simulation in ClayPantelegraphEngine (claymortal_web_system_v10.1.zip), the native Capacitor mobile bridge (capacitor.config.ts), and the Windows 11 PowerShell automation toolchain (install-crabdeck.ps1) certified in Section 447 of the Primary Project Checklist. Our focus is to eliminate stochastic scanline advancement bugs, cleartext mobile network vulnerabilities, stale asset build races, and background animation leaks.
The Roundtable
* The Integration Architect (Systems & Data Flow):
   * Stochastic Scanline Advance Flaw in ClayPantelegraphEngine: In main.js (lines 35105–35120), scanlines advance via const atEdge = Math.abs(this.pendulumAngle) > this.pendulumAmplitude * 0.96; if (atEdge && Math.random() < 0.25) this.currentScanline++. Because atEdge remains true across 8–15 frames near the pendulum's turning points, relying on a pseudo-random probability check creates severe frame-rate dependent distortion: at 120 FPS, the scanline can increment 3–4 times during a single pendulum reversal (causing skipped scanlines and compressed vertical artifacts), while at 30 FPS, it frequently fails to advance at all. The scanline increment must be governed by a deterministic peak velocity zero-crossing detector (this.lastVelocitySign !== currentVelocitySign) with a latch flag reset at center crossing.
   * Atomic Vite Build & Capacitor Sync Pipeline: In install-crabdeck.ps1, executing npx cap sync android before verifying the compilation hash of dist/ risks copying stale web bundles into native Android assets. The installer must enforce an atomic sequence: npm run build with exit code verification, followed immediately by npx cap sync android and APK compilation.
* The Permissions Guard / Red Teamer (Security, Privacy & Blast Radius):
   * Capacitor cleartext: true Production Leak: In capacitor.config.ts, server.cleartext: true is enabled to allow the Android WebView to communicate with local development gateways (http://127.0.0.1:8000 / http://10.0.2.2:8000). If compiled into a production release without conditional gating, the application will allow unencrypted HTTP traffic over untrusted networks. Gating cleartext strictly to development environments (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') or injecting a build-time flag (CAPACITOR_CLEARTEXT=true) is essential to prevent man-in-the-middle data interception.
   * Process-Scoped PowerShell Execution: Confirms that restricting execution policy to -Scope Process RemoteSigned in install-crabdeck.ps1 prevents altering host-wide system security configurations on chase2x2.
* The Cognitive Load Analyst / End-User (UX, Friction & Reporting):
